Infer ``None`` for the ``fset`` of a property declared with ``@property`` and no
``.setter``, as CPython does, instead of raising. The lookup escaped as a bare
``StopIteration`` and was reported as a crash on code as simple as ``C.p.fset``.
Properties built by a ``property(...)`` call are left as they were: the setter
argument is not modelled, so ``fset`` stays uninferable rather than being reported
as ``None``.

Closes pylint-dev/pylint#8739
